{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "c9f2d4ab-reject-matrix-0001",
		"name": "SignFlow Rejection Matrix",
		"description": "Exercises every server-side rejection path of the coordination API.\n\nSETUP FIRST (one command, server must already be running):\n  powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File postman/setup-rejection-matrix.ps1\n\nIt creates a dedicated 2-signer workflow, downloads revision 0, builds the tampered fixtures and writes fixtures/matrix-env.json. Import that as a Postman ENVIRONMENT and select it. Then run this collection top to bottom: every request asserts its exact expected status code AND error code, so the whole suite should show green.\n\nWhat is covered: JWT enforcement, participant authorization, turn enforcement, stale parent revision, stale parent hash, byte-prefix tampering, chain-breaking append, unsigned resubmission, missing/short fingerprint validation, idempotency replay. NOT covered from raw HTTP: a cryptographically valid signature from a DIFFERENT certificate (needs the desktop app's PKCS#11 signing - see the 'Wrong certificate' request's description for the manual repro).",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"variable": [
		{ "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:8080" },
		{ "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "refreshToken", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "workflowId", "value": "SET_BY_SETUP_SCRIPT" },
		{ "key": "parentRevision", "value": "0" },
		{ "key": "parentSha256", "value": "SET_BY_SETUP_SCRIPT" },
		{ "key": "operationId", "value": "SET_BY_SETUP_SCRIPT" }
	],
